I haven't worked out how to have comments in the included style file mymacros.sty
So the version with commentary is here.

1) File `mymacros.sty` defines LaTeX macros to be read by MathJax in the HTML output.
2) File `include-in-header.tex` (which lives in the main directory) defines LaTeX macros to be read by LaTeX in the PDF output.
3) You need to add new macros to both (a quirk of Quarto as of 2026, still)

% This is used for pdf compilation from qmd.
% This file should be updated in parallel with mymacros.sty which is used for html compilation.
% This is how the two files are included in the _quarto.yaml header of the qmd file
%format:
%  html:
%    defaults: [mymacros.sty]
%  pdf:
%   include-in-header: ["include-in-header.tex"]

% Here are the default commands I've included with the template:

\newcommand*{\diff}[3][]{\frac{\!\textrm{d}^{#1} #2}{\textrm{d}#3^{#1}}}

% Declaring math operators. Could also use \newcommand{\name}{\operatorname{name}}
\DeclareMathOperator{\cosec}{cosec}
\DeclareMathOperator{\powop}{pow}
\DeclareMathOperator{\Bernoulli}{Bernoulli}
\DeclareMathOperator{\Binomial}{Binomial}
\DeclareMathOperator{\Multinomial}{Multinomial}
\DeclareMathOperator{\Multinom}{Multinom}
\DeclareMathOperator{\Bin}{Bin}
\DeclareMathOperator{\Poisson}{Poisson}

$\definecolor{frog}{rgb}{1,0,0}$
$\newcommand{\dx}{\,\text{d}x}$
$\newcommand{\du}{\,\text{d}u}$
$\newcommand{\dy}{\,\text{d}y}$
$\newcommand{\dt}{\,\text{d}t}$
